  m_Name: 1990 mrt
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  title: No Eating or Drinking on MRT 1990s
  info: Eating and drinking on MRT trains and in stations are prohibited to keep
    public transport clean and pleasant for all commuters. The rule is strictly enforced,
    with first-time offenders facing fines of up to SGD 500. The policy extends to
    items like water bottles and snacks, with signs and announcements reminding passengers
    of the rule. The initiative is part of a broader effort to create a comfortable
    and efficient public transport system.
  image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 58af6bf9173604169b57d964c59ee1f1, type: 3}
